hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1112","Chapter on detachments returning spoils to the main army, 1151 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslims' blood is equal in value, the lowest of them strives to grant protection on their behalf, the furthest of them grants refuge on their behalf, they are one hand against others, the strong among them returns spoils to the weak, and their raiding parties return to those who stayed behind. A believer is not killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while his covenant lasts."
